WEBVTT

00:04:56.916 --> 00:05:00.156
it slows down for a little while
and then just shoots off into space.

00:05:00.196 --> 00:05:01.716
It’s very similar physics,

00:05:01.756 --> 00:05:04.876
and we didn't have any idea
why that should happen.

00:05:05.556 --> 00:05:07.636
So we still don't know
why that's happening.

00:05:07.676 --> 00:05:11.076
We attribute it to something
we call “dark energy.”

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:12.716
We don't know what dark energy is.

00:05:12.756 --> 00:05:15.636
It's just something that seems
to be pushing things apart,

00:05:15.676 --> 00:05:17.916
making the universe expand faster.

00:05:17.956 --> 00:05:22.556
And because of that,
it looks like we will end up

00:05:22.596 --> 00:05:25.316
with everything, really --

00:05:25.356 --> 00:05:27.356
you know, all the galaxies
really isolated,

00:05:27.396 --> 00:05:29.636
the stars will die away.

00:05:29.676 --> 00:05:32.116
The universe will get
very dark, very cold.